* opamp_core unity-gain-buffer DC transfer testbench, `klt sim` circuit BODY (issue #77)
*
* Fleet-executable twin of opamp_dc_swing.spice.tmpl. Same follower
* connection (Rshort 1 mOhm out->inn) and the same input grid: the swept
* source Vsw runs 0 -> 1 in 1/360 steps and Bin scales it by each corner's own
* VDD (`alter vdd`), so v(inp) = VDD * k/360 exactly as the original's
* `dc Vinp 0 VDD VDD/360`. The sweep itself is returned as a waveform artifact
* (options.waveforms) and bin/pvt_sweep.py applies the unchanged slope-window
* rule (largest contiguous run around mid-supply with 0.8 <= dVout/dVin <= 1.2)
* to it -- a contiguous-run search cannot be expressed as a .meas card.

.option scale=1u

.subckt opamp_dut vdd vss inn inp out ibias
.include "{OPAMP_NETLIST}"
.ends opamp_dut

Vdd vdd 0 dc {VDD_NOM}
Vss vss 0 dc 0
Iref vdd ibias dc {IBIAS_A}
Xdut vdd vss inn inp out ibias opamp_dut
Rshort inn out 1m
Vsw sw 0 dc 0
Bin inp 0 V = v(vdd)*v(sw)
Cload out 0 {CL_F}
